---
import { getCollection } from "astro:content";
import ProgramPage from "../../layouts/ProgramPage.astro";

const greenhouseGasesPosts = await getCollection("programPost", ({ data }) => {
  return data.programArea.includes("Greenhouse Gases");
});

const pageTitle = "Greenhouse Gases";

const greenhouseGasesAreas = [
  {
    title: "Regulations, Guidance, and Policy",
    children: [
      { title: "National", url: "" },
      { title: "International", url: "" },
      { title: "Regional", url: "" },
    ],
  },

  {
    title: "Supporting Information and Tools",
    url: "",
    children: [
      { title: "Databases and Software Tools", url: "" },
      { title: "Directories, Catalogs, and Newsletters", url: "" },
      { title: "Libraries and Repositories", url: "" },
      { title: "Organizations and Programs", url: "" },
    ],
  },

  {
    title: "Lessons Learned",
    url: "",
    children: [
      { title: "Case Studies", url: "" },
      { title: "Inventories", url: "" },
    ],
  },

  { title: "Training, Presentations, and Briefings", url: "" },
  { title: "Conferences and Events", url: "" },
];
---

<ProgramPage
  programAreas={greenhouseGasesAreas}
  posts={greenhouseGasesPosts}
  pageTitle={pageTitle}
>
  <p>
    The Greenhouse Gases (GHG) Program Area includes the latest guidance and
    information resources to aid Federal facilities in managing greenhouse gas
    emissions. This encompasses current guidance, policies, and trends related
    to climate change/global warming, calculation of carbon footprints, and the
    application of offsets to reduce carbon footprints.
  </p>
  <p>
    The primary 6 GHGs of concern are: <b>carbon dioxide</b>, <b>methane</b>, <b
      >nitrous oxide</b
    >, <b>hydrofluorocarbons</b>, <b>perfluorocarbons</b>, and <b
      >sulfur hexafluoride</b
    >. The main sources of these gases due to human activity are as follows:
  </p>
  <ul class="usa-list">
    <li>
      Carbon Dioxide (CO<sub>2</sub>): burning of fossil fuels and
      deforestation;
    </li>
    <li>
      Methane (CH<sub>4</sub>): livestock enteric fermentation (i.e. cows) and
      manure management, paddy rice farming, land use and wetland changes,
      pipeline losses, and covered vented landfill emissions;
    </li>
    <li>
      Hydrofluorocarbons (HFCs): these items are of concern from the standpoint
      of global warming and the Kyoto Protocol;
    </li>
    <li>
      Perfluorocarbons (PFCs): these are being used in refrigerating units as
      replacements for CFCs;
    </li>
    <li>
      Nitrous Oxide (N<sub>2</sub>O): this is used for its anesthetic and
      analgesic effects as well as being used as an oxidizer in rocketry and in
      motor racing to increase the power output of engines;
    </li>
    <li>
      Sulfur Hexafluoride (SF<sub>6</sub>): used in the electrical industry as a
      gaseous dielectric medium for high-voltage (35 kV and above) circuit
      breakers, switchgear, and other electrical equipment, often referred to as
      SF<sub>6</sub>. SF<sub>6</sub> is also employed as a contrast agent for ultrasound
      imaging. See the <a
        href="https://www.fedcenter.gov/_kd/go.cfm?destination=ShowItem&Item_ID=13856"
        target="new">DOE Safety Bulletin</a
      > for more information on SF<sub>6</sub>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    When future Executive Orders (EOs) and Implementing Instructions for those
    EOs are released addressing federal facilities the text on this page will be
    updated.
  </p>
</ProgramPage>
